From 34517acef891e2fb3fb389ff7c997ed0b8d40a65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mansur Aliyu <mansurmasama@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:43:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix transaction gossip, fork resolution and selfish miner;
 add transaction window

Prepared with Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) and checked by test runs of the
simulator before and after the changes.

Simulator fixes (3sim core):
- Transaction gossip: a node kept only one receive callback, so received
  transactions were never forwarded (they reached ~1-5% of nodes).
- Fork resolution: the common ancestor of the old and new chain was computed
  from stale state, so canonical blocks could be typed stale.
- Selfish miner: the attacker detached from the network and stopped seeing
  honest blocks, so SPSM was ~0.

Transaction window (manuscript Section V):
- Submission starts kappa_tx_warm = 30 canonical blocks before measurement and
  stops after K_tx = min(100, kappa_measure * N_V) measurement blocks.
- TPS is evaluated over those K_tx blocks (distinct transactions in
  majority-canonical measurement blocks / window duration); TCR and CL over the
  transactions submitted in them. Block metrics use all kappa_measure * N_V
  blocks.
- Config keys transaction_warmup_blocks (default 30) and
  transaction_measurement_blocks_max (default 100; 0 = legacy behaviour).
- New audit fields transactionWindow* in the result JSON.

Inputs and checks:
- Loader records lambda_tx_effective; accepts number_of_attackers when
  fraction_of_attackers is absent.
- verify_pilot_results.py checks gossip coverage, lambda_tx_effective and the
  transaction window.
- generate_execution_manifests.py: revised generator (absolute rate, Eq. 7,
  renamed inputs accepted).

